      "hints": [
        "Substitute $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ into $3\\cos\\theta = 8\\tan\\theta$.",
        "Multiply across by $\\cos\\theta$ and replace $\\cos^2\\theta$ with $1 - \\sin^2\\theta$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ into the given equation:\n$$3\\cos\\theta = 8\\left(\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\right)$$",
        "Multiply through by $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$3\\cos^2\\theta = 8\\sin\\theta$$",
        "Use the Pythagorean identity $\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta$ and rearrange into standard quadratic form:\n$$3(1 - \\sin^2\\theta) = 8\\sin\\theta \\implies 3 - 3\\sin^2\\theta = 8\\sin\\theta$$\n$$3\\sin^2\\theta + 8\\sin\\theta - 3 = 0$$"
      ],
